IMPORT prelude

-- Land Betterment Charge Act 2021 (Singapore) -- who counts as an owner (s 4), which method fixes the charge and when it is nil
-- (ss 8(2), 9, 10(3), 11(1), (2)), deferment for charities (ss 20(2)(a), (3), (4), 22(4)), the 24-month window for revising a
-- liability order (ss 25(4), 27(2)), short levies (s 30), insolvency priority (s 33), contribution between co-payers, tenants and
-- portions of land (ss 34, 35, 36(2)), refunds (s 37(3)), penalty tax for unauthorised development (ss 41 to 43), the rectification
-- offence (s 40(7)), evasion (s 45(1)) and the appeal deadlines (s 47(2)).
--
-- Edition: informal consolidation, "version in force from 18/12/2023", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/LBCA2021.txt
-- (retrieved 1 October 2026, described by the deposit's metadata as the current version as at 01 Oct 2026). The latest
-- amendment annotated in the text is Act 23 of 2023 wef 18/12/2023 (ss 2, 8(3)(d), (e), 26(2)(d)).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0069 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. SCOPED to the provisions an owner, co-owner, tenant, charity or developer actually meets. Not
-- encoded: the meaning of "chargeable consent" and the ordering of multiple events (s 3), the relevant point in time (s 8(3), (4)),
-- the content of the pre- and post-chargeable valuations (s 11(3) to (6)), the prescribed percentages and Table of Rates (in
-- Regulations, not deposited), exemptions and concessionary relief (ss 12, 13), remission (s 14), assumption of liability and
-- transfer of deferred liability (ss 16, 23) beyond a comment, interest at the prescribed rate (s 38), administration and
-- enforcement powers (Part 8 except s 54), and the amendments and transitional provisions (Part 10).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Land Betterment Charge Act 2021 -- charge and liability`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `4 -- material interest and owner`

-- s 4(1): "a person is not an owner of any land unless the person has a material interest in the land."
-- s 4(2): a material interest is a legal interest that is (a) an estate in fee simple; (b) an estate in perpetuity; (c) "a leasehold
-- estate under a State title of whatever tenure"; or (d) an interest entitling the person to receive rent if the land is let "for more
-- than 10 years"; "and includes a mortgagee in possession".
-- s 4(3)(a): an option to extend "exercisable wholly at the lessee's discretion" counts towards the term; (b) a break on the happening
-- of an event does not shorten it.
-- s 4(4): a buyer of a lot "from a developer" of a strata development "before that completion" is not, by reason only of that, a holder
-- of a material interest.
DECLARE Interest IS ONE OF
    `an estate in fee simple`
    `an estate in perpetuity`
    `a leasehold estate under a State title`
    `a right to receive rent under a letting`
    `a mortgagee in possession`
    `a mortgagee not in possession`
    `a buyer of an uncompleted strata lot from the developer`
    `a tenant under a private lease`

GIVEN `the interest` IS A Interest, `letting term in years` IS A NUMBER, `lessee's option years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interest is material` IF
    CONSIDER `the interest`
    WHEN `an estate in fee simple` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an estate in perpetuity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a leasehold estate under a State title` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a right to receive rent under a letting` THEN `letting term in years` PLUS `lessee's option years` GREATER THAN 10
    WHEN `a mortgagee in possession` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `8(2), 9, 10(3), 11(1) and (2) -- which method, and when the charge is nil`

-- s 9(1): the charge is ascertained by the Table of Rates method unless s 9(2) applies.
-- s 9(2): the VALUATION method is used for (a) varying "a special condition in a directly allotted State title", but not "a development
-- of land without a material change of use" nor a directly allotted (non-concessional) title "granted to a public authority"; or (b)
-- varying "a restrictive covenant in a concessional State title", "a controlled activity restrictive covenant" or "a subdivision
-- control restrictive covenant". s 8(2) gives the same list a prescribed percentage that "is higher than" the s 8(1) percentage.
-- s 9(3): the Valuation method may be used instead of the Table of Rates where "(a) all taxable persons concerned elect, before a
-- liability order is given" or "(b) the Table of Rates method is inapplicable". s 9(5): the election "is irrevocable".
DECLARE Consent IS ONE OF
    `a planning permission`
    `a conservation permission`
    `acceptance of a lodgment of deemed-authorised plans`
    `varying a development control covenant`
    `varying a special condition in a directly allotted title`
    `varying a covenant in a concessional title`
    `varying a controlled activity covenant`
    `varying a subdivision control covenant`

GIVEN `the consent` IS A Consent, `there is a material change of use` IS A BOOLEAN, `the title was granted to a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consent is in the section 9(2) list` IF
    CONSIDER `the consent`
    WHEN `varying a special condition in a directly allotted title` THEN `there is a material change of use` AND (NOT `the title was granted to a public authority`)
    WHEN `varying a covenant in a concessional title` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `varying a controlled activity covenant` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `varying a subdivision control covenant` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the consent` IS A Consent, `there is a material change of use` IS A BOOLEAN, `the title was granted to a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `all taxable persons elected in time` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Table of Rates is inapplicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Valuation method is used` IF
        `the consent is in the section 9(2) list` `the consent` `there is a material change of use` `the title was granted to a public authority`
    OR  `all taxable persons elected in time`
    OR  `the Table of Rates is inapplicable`

GIVEN `the consent` IS A Consent, `there is a material change of use` IS A BOOLEAN, `the title was granted to a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the higher prescribed percentage applies` IF
    `the consent is in the section 9(2) list` `the consent` `there is a material change of use` `the title was granted to a public authority`

-- s 11(1): the Table of Rates method derives the post- and pre-chargeable valuations from prescribed rates and then subtracts "the
-- pre-chargeable valuation of the land from the post-chargeable valuation". s 11(2): no charge "where the post-chargeable valuation of
-- the land does not exceed the pre-chargeable valuation". (The rates themselves are in Regulations, not deposited; the valuations are
-- inputs here.)
GIVEN `post-chargeable valuation` IS A NUMBER, `pre-chargeable valuation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Table of Rates charge` MEANS
    IF `post-chargeable valuation` GREATER THAN `pre-chargeable valuation`
    THEN `post-chargeable valuation` MINUS `pre-chargeable valuation`
    ELSE 0

-- s 10(3): no charge by the Valuation method where "the price the land might reasonably obtain if sold at the relevant point in time
-- ... does not exceed the price if sold before that relevant point in time".
GIVEN `price at the relevant point in time` IS A NUMBER, `price before it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no charge is payable by valuation` IF
    `price at the relevant point in time` AT MOST `price before it`

§§ `15, 16 and 18 -- who pays`

-- s 15(1): payable by (a) "every person who, when the chargeable consent is given, is an owner of the land"; (b) anyone who gives an
-- assumption of liability notice; (c) a transferee of deferred liability. s 15(2): liability "continues despite the taxable person
-- disposing of the land". s 16(1)(b): a notice may NOT be given "after a revised liability order is given"; s 16(6) it is
-- irrevocable; s 16(7) the default taxable person "then ceases to be liable". s 18(1): joint owners of a material interest are
-- "jointly and severally liable".
GIVEN `owned a material interest when the consent was given` IS A BOOLEAN, `has since sold the land` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `someone assumed the liability in place of this owner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner is liable` IF
    `owned a material interest when the consent was given` AND (NOT `someone assumed the liability in place of this owner`)

GIVEN `a revised liability order has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an assumption of liability notice may still be given` IF
    NOT `a revised liability order has been given`

§§ `20(2)(a), (3), (4) and 22(4) -- deferment for charities`

-- s 20(2)(a): the Authority may defer where "the taxable person is a charitable institution and the land will be used wholly or mainly
-- for charitable purposes". s 20(3): not so where the material interest is owned "jointly with a person who is not a charitable
-- institution". s 20(4): charitable use "includes leaving it unoccupied". The grant is discretionary ("may"); this decides only
-- eligibility on this ground (s 20(2)(b) criteria are in Regulations, not deposited).
-- s 22(4)(c): before cancelling, the Authority must allow "not less than 7 days" for written representations.
GIVEN `is a charitable institution` IS A BOOLEAN, `land used wholly or mainly for charitable purposes` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `land left unoccupied` IS A BOOLEAN, `owned jointly with a non-charity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible for deferment as a charity` IF
        `is a charitable institution`
    AND (`land used wholly or mainly for charitable purposes` OR `land left unoccupied`)
    AND (NOT `owned jointly with a non-charity`)

GIVEN `days allowed for representations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cancellation notice allows enough time` IF
    `days allowed for representations` AT LEAST 7

§§ `25(4) and 27(2) -- the 24-month window`

-- s 27(2): no revised liability order on the Authority's own initiative "if more than 24 months has lapsed after" the (last) date the
-- chargeable consent was given. s 25(4): an ESTIMATED liability order "is treated as final" when "24 months has lapsed" and "no revised
-- liability order is earlier given" -- subject to s 30 (short levy). Months are whole numbers here. At exactly 24 months both tests are
-- met on this reading (revision not yet barred, estimate already final); that overlap is an inference from the wording, not stated.
GIVEN `months since the consent was last given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may still revise on its own initiative` IF
    `months since the consent was last given` AT MOST 24

GIVEN `months since the consent was last given` IS A NUMBER, `a revised liability order was given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the estimate is final` IF
    `months since the consent was last given` AT LEAST 24 AND (NOT `a revised liability order was given`)

§§ `30 -- short levy and erroneous refund`

-- s 30(2): a demand is valid if "(a) it is in writing; (b) it is made within 2 years after the date of payment"; (c) it specifies the
-- amount or circumstances. s 30(3): the 2-year limit does not apply to "fraud or evasion". s 30(4): where the amount "does not exceed
-- $20" the Authority may waive recovery.
GIVEN `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `months since payment` IS A NUMBER, `fraud or evasion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the short-levy demand is valid` IF
    `in writing` AND (`months since payment` AT MOST 24 OR `fraud or evasion`)

GIVEN `the shortfall` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `recovery of the shortfall may be waived` IF
    `the shortfall` AT MOST 20

§§ `33 -- priority in insolvency`

-- s 33(1), (2): a charge or penalty tax "due ... at the date of the bankruptcy order" (or winding up order) and "having become due within
-- 12 months before" ranks among the priority debts under ss 352 and 203 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018.
GIVEN `due at the date of the order` IS A BOOLEAN, `months it had been due before the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the charge has priority in insolvency` IF
    `due at the date of the order` AND `months it had been due before the order` AT MOST 12

§§ `34, 35 and 36(2) -- who bears it in the end`

-- s 34(a): one who pays the whole may recover from each other person jointly liable an amount in "the same proportion as the value of
-- the estate or interest in the land of the other person bears to the total of the values".
GIVEN `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER, `value of the other person's interest` IS A NUMBER, `total value of all interests` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the contribution recoverable` MEANS
    `the amount paid` TIMES `value of the other person's interest` DIVIDED BY `total value of all interests`

-- s 35(1)(a): on default, a lessee or occupier "is responsible for the payment" as if the defaulting taxable person; s 35(2) "limited
-- to any rent or payments due by the lessee or occupier to the taxable person at the time of demand".
GIVEN `the unpaid charge` IS A NUMBER, `rent due to the taxable person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tenant's responsibility` MEANS
    `the lesser of` `the unpaid charge` `rent due to the taxable person`

-- s 36(1): the charge is "a first charge on that land in priority over all other encumbrances whatever". s 36(2): on disposing of a
-- portion, the portion bears the total charge in proportion to "the area of that portion" to "the area of the whole parcel", and the
-- remainder bears the difference.
GIVEN `the total charge` IS A NUMBER, `area of the portion` IS A NUMBER, `area of the whole parcel` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the charge on the portion` MEANS
    `the total charge` TIMES `area of the portion` DIVIDED BY `area of the whole parcel`

GIVEN `the total charge` IS A NUMBER, `area of the portion` IS A NUMBER, `area of the whole parcel` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the charge on the remainder` MEANS
    `the total charge` MINUS `the charge on the portion` `the total charge` `area of the portion` `area of the whole parcel`

§§ `37(3) -- refunds`

-- s 37(1), (2): an overpayment, or a payment for a consent never "eventually given", must be refunded. s 37(3): the refund "must be
-- claimed in writing ... within 6 years starting the date the liability order ... becomes final and conclusive". Counted in whole
-- months here (72); the exact end of the 6 years is not tested.
GIVEN `claimed in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `months since the order became final` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the refund claim is in time` IF
    `claimed in writing` AND `months since the order became final` LESS THAN 72

§§ `41, 42 and 43 -- penalty tax for unauthorised development`

-- s 41(1): penalty tax on a rectification order is "(a) the amount of the land betterment charge that would have been payable" plus
-- "(b) 30% of the amount in paragraph (a)". s 41(2): none if it happened "solely because of circumstances beyond the tax payer's
-- control ... but not amounting to financial incapacity"; s 41(3) "it is for the tax payer to prove" that.
-- s 42: the Authority "may" use (a) 6% if the tax payer discloses in writing BEFORE being told of an investigation; (b) 24% if after
-- being told and "before the investigation is begun". s 43: the Authority "may" use 50% if the tax payer "hinders or obstructs" an
-- officer or valuer before the investigation is completed. The reduced and increased rates are discretionary; this encoding gives the
-- rate where the Authority exercises its power.
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `no disclosure and no obstruction`
    `disclosed before being told of an investigation`
    `disclosed after being told but before it began`
    `disclosed after the investigation began`
    `obstructed the investigation`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the penalty percentage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `disclosed before being told of an investigation` THEN 6
    WHEN `disclosed after being told but before it began` THEN 24
    WHEN `obstructed the investigation` THEN 50
    OTHERWISE 30

GIVEN `the notional charge` IS A NUMBER, `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `proved circumstances beyond control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the penalty tax` MEANS
    IF `proved circumstances beyond control`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the notional charge` PLUS `the notional charge` TIMES `the penalty percentage` `the conduct` DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `40(7), 45(1) and 54 -- offences`

-- s 40(7): failing without reasonable excuse to comply with a restoration order: "a fine not exceeding $200,000 or ... imprisonment for
-- a term not exceeding 12 months or ... both", and for a continuing offence "a further fine not exceeding $10,000 for every day or part
-- of a day" after conviction.
GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for not restoring the land` MEANS
    200000 PLUS 10000 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

-- s 45(1): wilful evasion (false statement, false answer, "fraud, art or contrivance"): "a penalty of 4 times the amount of land
-- betterment charge which has been underpaid" AND a fine not exceeding $50,000 or imprisonment up to 5 years or both. s 45(2): a false
-- entry is presumed made "with intent to evade" until the contrary is proved.
GIVEN `the amount underpaid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the evasion penalty` MEANS
    4 TIMES `the amount underpaid`

-- s 54(1): failing without reasonable excuse to give information required under s 17(2), 52(1) or 53: fine up to $10,000. s 54(4):
-- self-incrimination "is a reasonable excuse". s 54(3): defence of not possessing it after all reasonable steps.
GIVEN `failed to give required information` IS A BOOLEAN, `it might tend to incriminate` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved it was unobtainable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to give information is an offence` IF
    `failed to give required information` AND (NOT `it might tend to incriminate`) AND (NOT `proved it was unobtainable`)

§§ `47(2) and 48 -- appeal to the Minister`

-- s 47(2): an appeal against "a liability order or revised liability order" within "30 days after the date the decision ... is given";
-- for any other appealable decision (refusing or cancelling a deferment, refusing a transfer of deferred liability, a rectification
-- order) "within 14 days". s 47(5): the Minister's decision "is final". s 48: an appeal "does not affect the operation of the
-- appealable decision" -- the charge must still be paid.
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `a liability order`
    `a revised liability order`
    `a refusal to defer`
    `a cancellation of a deferment`
    `a refusal to approve a transfer of deferred liability`
    `a rectification order`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the appeal period in days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a liability order` THEN 30
    WHEN `a revised liability order` THEN 30
    OTHERWISE 14

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision, `days since the decision was given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
    `days since the decision was given` AT MOST `the appeal period in days` `the decision`
